    {
      "id": "claim_8188bb6e070e4cc1a11ca9dabc5c0338",
      "statement": "The shared cached test task exists because vp declines to cache a task that reads a path it also wrote; vitest's scratch paths (node_modules/.vite results.json, node_modules/.vite-temp config temp modules, .wrangler validate tree) are excluded workspace-wide because tracking reaches past the owning package and siblings would otherwise invalidate each other, and vp run --last-details names the offending path when a task stops caching.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L41-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53fb5d47a07018534ab7d0e9228ee88fae816e3f1c7eff02e4fa81baf8444f9c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_42db3217267f4fefb091b36923ffa9cf",
      "statement": "Every vitest command in the shared test task runs under scripts/with-timeout.ts because nothing else bounds a wedged run: vitest timeouts die with the test worker, Vite+ has no task timeout, and vitest-pool-workers imports Miniflare without a crash-restart hook so a dead workerd leaves the pool awaiting forever; the watchdog uses 60s of silence (a healthy run prints per file) plus a 600s cap, kills the entire process tree, and exits 124 (GNU timeout's code).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/with-timeout.ts#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:43f394f61cefb6033bfcd752973b9cc40dd8f33c4fa28ed928a94aaca792632d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d784a9a9bad64c1991a9ee6fd446d084",
      "statement": "The watchdog thresholds are baked into the command string rather than read from the environment because the command is part of the cache fingerprint and a cached vp run strips undeclared env vars — a threshold override would silently not apply, so a policy change is a visible fingerprinted change.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L75-L100",
